# Re-include this folder's Markdown. The repo-root .gitignore blanket-ignores
# `*.md` at every depth, and `common_setup96` dropped the negations that used to
# rescue app docs — so without this file every design note, decisions log and
# session record written here is invisible to `git add`.
#
# This is not hypothetical: twelve QuikPilot docs were swallowed exactly this way
# and had to be recovered with `git add -f`. A doc that silently never gets
# committed reads as "written" right up until someone else clones the repo.
#
# Why the negation is honoured: a nested .gitignore takes precedence over the
# parent for the paths it covers, and the root's `*.md` matches FILES, not the
# `Quikpilot_docs/` directory — an ignored directory would never be descended
# into and no negation inside it could win. Same mechanism as
# `apps/quikchat/.gitignore`.
#
# Scoped to this folder and below. The root rule still holds everywhere else.
!*.md
